Benchmark 2: Compute-Heavy (N = 2^24 elements, 64-iteration inner loop)
  - PTX Instruction Counts:
      MiniPTX:                    54 instructions
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):            28 instructions
  - SASS Instruction Counts:
      MiniPTX:                    24 SASS instructions
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):            32 SASS instructions
  - Measured Runtime (Median):
      MiniPTX:                    0.4721 ms
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):            0.4209 ms
  - Computed Throughput:
      MiniPTX:                    4549 GFLOPS
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):            5103 GFLOPS
  - Measured Ratio:
      MiniPTX / CUDA:             1.122x (MiniPTX is 12.17% slower)

Notes on Instruction Counts & Performance:
  - In SAXPY, MiniPTX produces 24 SASS instructions vs 16 for CUDA, but both achieve
    identical runtime (0.2570 ms / 783.3 GB/s) because memory traffic saturates the
    Volta HBM2 DRAM subsystem.
  - In Compute-Heavy, MiniPTX produces fewer static SASS instructions (24 vs 32), yet
    runs 12.17% slower. Static instruction counts do not equal executed instructions
    when loops, instruction scheduling, and hardware FMA fusion are involved.
